Mechanism: Both changes act on attention behavior. RoPE, inserted into a char-based Transformer, is reported to give better results than the baseline Transformer. QK-normalization is reported to keep attention stacks trainable and to mitigate degradation, so it may stabilize the rotated query-key logits at the relatively high learning rate. Together they may let attention fit the data more efficiently within a short training budget.
